The evaluation corpus tests/gold.jsonl (not part of the runtime image) contains
coordinates, administrative codes and addresses derived from:
- Wikidata (CC0-1.0) and the Dutch BAG via PDOK (CC0-1.0);
- Base Adresse Nationale, licensed under Licence Ouverte / Open Licence 2.0
  (https://www.etalab.gouv.fr/licence-ouverte-open-licence/);
- the US Census Bureau geocoder (US Government work, public domain);
- the ONS Postcode Directory via postcodes.io, licensed under the Open
  Government Licence v3.0 (https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/).
  Contains OS data © Crown copyright and database right. Contains Royal Mail
  data © Royal Mail copyright and database right. Source: Office for National Statistics.
Per-case sources and retrieval dates are recorded in the corpus; `evaluate build-gold` regenerates it
from tests/gold.seeds.jsonl.

The registry-first sample tests/registry/us.jsonl contains addresses and coordinates from the US
Department of Transportation's National Address Database (release r24), a work of the United States
government in the public domain. The data is provided as is, without warranty of accuracy, and is
not for use as a mailing list.

The registry-first sample tests/registry/fr.jsonl contains addresses and coordinates from the
Base Adresse Nationale export of 2026-10-16, under Licence Ouverte / Open Licence 2.0
(https://www.etalab.gouv.fr/licence-ouverte-open-licence/). Source: Base Adresse Nationale and
its contributing municipalities, https://adresse.data.gouv.fr/. Per-case export checksums and
retrieval dates are recorded in the corpus.

The registry-first sample tests/registry/no.jsonl contains addresses and coordinates from
Kartverket's Matrikkelen - Adresse national CSV export of 2026-10-10. © Kartverket,
licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
Dataset: https://kartkatalog.geonorge.no/metadata/uuid/f7df7a18-b30f-4745-bd64-d0863812350c.
Queries include constructed variants; per-case export checksums and retrieval dates are recorded
in the corpus. The data is provided as is, without a guarantee of accuracy.

The registry-first sample tests/registry/ch.jsonl contains addresses and coordinates derived from
the official directory of building addresses, ©swisstopo (Federal Office of Topography swisstopo),
STAC item dated 2026-10-16. LV95 points were converted to WGS84 with swisstopo's REFRAME service.
Use, redistribution, processing and commercial use are permitted with source attribution under
https://www.swisstopo.admin.ch/ogd-conditions. Queries include constructed variants; per-case
export checksums, retrieval dates and coordinate-conversion provenance are recorded in the corpus.
The data is provided as is, without a guarantee of accuracy.

